## Test Smell Audit — `OrderProcessorTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 / .NET 10 | **Catalog:** testsmells.org 19-smell taxonomy

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 4 | 4 |
| Medium | 3 | 3 |
| Low | 1 | 8 (class-wide) |
| **Total** | **8** | **8 unique methods** |

---

### HIGH Severity

#### 1. Conditional Test Logic
**Method:** `ProcessOrder_SetsCorrectStatus` (line 24)
```csharp
if (result.TotalAmount > 100)
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
else
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
```
**Problem:** One branch never executes — the test always passes but only verifies one path.
**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_OverHundred_SetsPremiumStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-EXPENSIVE", 5) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_UnderHundred_SetsStandardStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-CHEAP", 1) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

---

#### 2. Assertion-Free Test (a.k.a. Unknown Test)
**Method:** `ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError` (line 43)
```csharp
processor.ProcessOrder(order);
// ← no assertion
```
**Problem:** The test passes even if the order is silently corrupted — any non-throwing bug is invisible.
**Fix:** Assert on the expected side-effect:
```csharp
var result = processor.ProcessOrder(order);
Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
Assert.IsTrue(_db.WasOrderSaved(order.Id));
```

---

#### 3. Sleepy Test
**Method:** `ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent` (line 91)
```csharp
Thread.Sleep(2000);
```
**Problem:** Adds 2 seconds of wall-clock time per run; may still race on slow CI agents.
**Fix:** Use a synchronization primitive or polling helper:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    await processor.ProcessOrderAsync(order);

    Assert.IsTrue(_email.WasNotificationSent(order.Id));
}
```
If the API is fire-and-forget, expose a `Task` or use `_email.WaitForNotification(timeout)`.

---

#### 4. Mystery Guest
**Method:** `ImportOrders_FromCsv_ParsesCorrectly` (line 140)
```csharp
File.ReadAllText(@"C:\TestData\orders.csv")
